      "trackName": "Duo Aquarium",
      "version": "1.1",
      "wrapperType": "software",
      "currency": "USD",
      "description": "A living aquarium that changes with iPhone Duo. Fold it part-way for your desk. Open it flat to explore the tank. Choose the fish, plant a freshwater scene or build a reef, and share the view with someone else.\n\nDESIGNED FOR iPhone Duo\n• Fold part-way into a tabletop position to enter Desk view automatically. The aquarium and clock stay above the hinge, with feeding, lighting and aquarium controls below.\n• Open the device flat to return from automatic Desk view to the full aquarium.\n• The native layout responds to the hinge and keeps controls clear of the fold.\n• On other iPhones, iPad and Mac, enjoy the aquarium and Desk view in their own screen layouts.\n\nBUILD YOUR AQUARIUM\n• Choose freshwater and reef fish, from shoaling tetras and angelfish to clownfish, tangs and gobies.\n• Add plants, corals, anemones, rocks and wood. Place coral on live rock and adjust your scenery.\n• Moving water, rippling light and real 3D scanned coral give the tank depth.\n• Feed your fish and watch them gather. Tap a resident or piece of scenery to identify it.\n• Take a clean picture of your tank with the controls hidden.\n\nA CLOCK BESIDE THE WATER\n• Desk view combines your aquarium with a clock, date and optional local weather.\n• Choose the clock's position, font and format, or show just the tank.\n• Switch between daybreak, daylight, moonlight and reef-blue lighting, with a daily light cycle and an evening dim.\n• Play optional calm music and water sound, or keep it silent.\n\nSHARE YOUR TANK\n• Let a friend visit using your tank code or link. They see your fish, scenery and lighting, while their own tank stays saved.\n• Place two nearby devices side by side and stretch one tank across them. Fish swim between the screens and either device can feed them.\n• Nearby sharing uses Wi-Fi or Bluetooth. Visiting a shared tank uses the internet; hosting requires iCloud.\n\nSMALL DAILY DETAILS\n• Home Screen and Lock Screen widgets show your tank and last feeding.\n• Set an optional daily feeding reminder, or feed through Siri and Shortcuts.\n• Keep the tank in a window or full screen on Mac.\n\nYour tank is saved on your device. No ads or tracking. Sharing stays off until you enable it, and you can stop it at any time.\n\niPhone Duo fold features require iOS 27.1 or later. iPhone, iPad and Mac are trademarks of Apple Inc. iPhone Duo is a trademark of Apple Inc.",
